    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T22:31:04Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 17a8c6e7: tracing the create/edit parameter types and OpFrame::of does not reproduce a tilted whole-model 3D Pocket without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nPocket3D has no tilt field. OpParams::tilt() explicitly returns None for Pocket3D and MultiAxisRough. OpFrame::of reads only op.params.tilt(), so neither kind can reach the tilted open-side branch through these commands.\n\nCommit 752d6c13 added the existing no_3d_pocket_kind_carries_a_tilt test and the defensive generator refusal for #1774. This is source inspection, not an executed test result. The requested early named refusal is not implemented, but its input state is currently unrepresentable. Adding a reachable failing pin would require extending the operation type first.\n\nStopped before claiming. No code changed.\n",
